### Role Management API Tests
### Test the role management endpoints for super admins

@baseUrl = http://localhost:1337
@adminToken = your-admin-jwt-token-here

### 1. Create a new admin role
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Content Manager",
  "description": "Manages content and user interactions",
  "type": "custom",
  "permissions": ["content_management", "user_read", "communication_access"]
}

### 2. List all admin roles
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 3. Update an admin role
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/roles/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Senior Content Manager",
  "description": "Senior level content management with additional permissions",
  "permissions": ["content_management", "user_management", "communication_access", "analytics_access"]
}

### 4. Assign role to user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/roles/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "1",
  "roleId": "2"
}

### 5. Remove role from user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/roles/remove
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "1"
}

### 6. Delete an admin role
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/roles/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 7. Test unauthorized access (should fail)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/roles
Authorization: Bearer invalid-token

### 8. Test with regular admin (should fail for super admin functions)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/roles
Authorization: Bearer regular-admin-token

